  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "what-is-c",
      "title": "What is C Language?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "isHtml": true,
          "text": "C is a <strong>general-purpose, procedural, high-level programming language</strong> developed by <strong>Dennis Ritchie</strong> at Bell Laboratories in 1972. It is one of the most influential programming languages ever created and forms the foundation of modern languages like C++, Java, Python, and Go."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "isHtml": true,
          "text": "C provides low-level access to memory through pointers while maintaining a simple and elegant syntax. It is widely used in <strong>system programming</strong>, operating systems, embedded systems, game engines, and performance-critical applications."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "history-of-c",
      "title": "History of C Language",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "isHtml": true,
          "text": "C was developed between 1969 and 1973 by Dennis Ritchie while working on the Unix operating system. It was created as a successor to the B language (developed by Ken Thompson). The name 'C' came after 'B' in the alphabet."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "features-of-c",
      "title": "Key Features of C",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "featureCards",
          "items": [
            { "icon": "⚡", "title": "Procedural Language", "text": "Follows step-by-step approach using functions" },
            { "icon": "📌", "title": "Fast & Efficient", "text": "Close to hardware with minimal runtime overhead" },
            { "icon": "🔧", "title": "Portable", "text": "Code can run on different machines with little modification" },
            { "icon": "🔗", "title": "Rich Library", "text": "Huge standard library support" },
            { "icon": "📍", "title": "Pointers", "text": "Direct memory access and manipulation" },
            { "icon": "🏗️", "title": "Modular", "text": "Supports functions and modular programming" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
