  "faq": {
    "sectionId": "faq-heading",
    "title": "Frequently Asked Questions — C Language",
    "items": [
      {
        "q": "Who developed C language?",
        "a": "Dennis Ritchie developed C at Bell Laboratories in 1972."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is C still used in 2026?",
        "a": "Yes. C is widely used in system programming, embedded systems, operating systems (Linux kernel), and performance-critical applications."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the difference between C and C++?",
        "a": "C++ is a superset of C with object-oriented features. C is procedural while C++ supports OOP, templates, STL, etc."
      }
    ]
